      "content": "Swelling and tenderness can be part of the body's response to a fungal infection, but a fever is a sign that your body is fighting something more serious. Ringworm itself doesn't usually cause a fever, so I would strongly advise against self-treatment. It's possible that you have a secondary bacterial infection or another issue that's causing these symptoms. I understand you want to avoid the clinic, but your health is at risk. If you really must avoid it, consider getting an over-the-counter antipyretic like acetaminophen to manage the fever and continue with the antifungal treatment. But please, don't ignore these signs. If the fever persists or the symptoms worsen, seek medical attention immediately. It's better to be safe than sorry.",
